    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup, serving as our highest-upside assets. **Gunnar Henderson** claims the top spot with a robust 76.64 score, buoyed significantly by a +16% park factor adjustment that maximizes his raw power profile. **Kyle Tucker** follows closely at 67.77; while facing the respectable arm of Brandon Sproat, **Kyle Tucker** maintains elite efficiency through consistent dynamic platoon advantages. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.00) also warrants attention as he projects for a strong outing against Mitch Keller, benefiting from an favorable 0.378 xwOBA that suggests he is primed to capitalize on the 3rd spot in the order.\n\nTactical adjustments highlight our approach to platoon splits and environmental factors today. **Sam Antonacci** (53.52) and **Miguel Vargas** (57.48) both receive a tangible boost from wind patterns blowing out, offsetting the inherent difficulty of facing southpaw Robbie Ray. Conversely, **Dominic Smith** sits at a marginal 41.03, tethered by a -9% penalty due to his same-handed matchup against Foster Griffin, keeping him firmly on the fringe of our starting requirements. The most difficult bench decision involved **Nolan Schanuel**, who posted a 49.36. While **Nolan Schanuel** was competitive, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Coby Mayo** (53.42) for the UTIL slot, as the latter\u2019s massive park factor advantage outweighed the stability offered by **Nolan Schanuel** against MacKenzie Gore.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, as this projection relies on anticipated batting orders. Any mid-day shakeup\u2014particularly if **Liam Hicks** or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** are shifted down in their respective lineups\u2014could quickly suppress their scores and force a re-evaluation of the bench. Furthermore, while **Andy Pages** (59.11) is a strong play, the elite hold percentage of his opposing pitcher poses a non-zero risk to our stolen base production for the day. Managers should verify confirmed lineups one hour prior to first pitch to ensure these projections hold.",
